## Architecture

```
Angular Dev Server (https://localhost:44426)
  ↓ proxy /api/** and /user/
.NET Backend (https://localhost:7123)
  ↓ port 6364
SSH Tunnel (localhost:6364)
  ↓ IAP bastion VM
Cloud SQL (10.129.0.16:5432)
```

## appsettings.json Configuration (Already Applied)

File: `UNOPS.PAO.Server/appsettings.json`

These values MUST be set for this developer:

```json
"ConnectionStrings": {
  "DbSchema": "public",
  "DbContext": "Host=127.0.0.1;Port=6364;Database=unops-opportunityplus-dev-db-emamirelar;Username=emamirelar@unops.org;",
  "UseIamAuthentication": true
}
```

```json
"Development": {
  "IAPSimulation": {
    "Enabled": true,
    "UserEmail": "emamirelar@unops.org",
    "SkipValidationInDevelopment": true
  }
}
```

If another developer's email appears in these fields, replace with the values above.

## Startup Sequence (3 Terminals)

### Terminal 1: SSH Tunnel to Cloud SQL

```bash
gcloud compute ssh unopsgc567901-sql-proxy \
  --tunnel-through-iap \
  --project=unops-opportunityplus-dev \
  --zone=europe-west4-b \
  --ssh-flag="-L 6364:10.129.0.16:5432" \
  --ssh-flag="-N"
```

- The `-N` flag keeps the tunnel open without executing a remote command (required for non-interactive shells)
- Verify with: `lsof -i :6364` — should show `ssh` listening
- **Keep this terminal open** for the duration of the session

### Terminal 2: .NET Backend

```bash
# From repo root:
dotnet watch run --project UNOPS.PAO.Server
```

- Listens on `https://localhost:7123` (HTTPS) and `http://localhost:5159` (HTTP)
- Swagger available at `https://localhost:7123/swagger`
- Hot reload enabled via `dotnet watch`

### Terminal 3: Angular Frontend

```bash
cd UNOPS.PAO.ClientApp
npm start
```

- Serves at `https://localhost:44426` (SSL)
- Proxy config in `UNOPS.PAO.ClientApp/src/proxy.conf.js` forwards `/api/**` and `/user/` to the backend
- Auto-login via IAP simulation as `emamirelar@unops.org`

